{
  "uid": "slos",
  "title": "SLOs",
  "tags": [
    "slo",
    "cerberus",
    "clickhouse"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 41,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "browser",
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "Span metrics (RED)",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/d/span-metrics-red",
      "keepTime": true,
      "includeVars": true,
      "icon": "dashboard"
    }
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "allValue": ".*",
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "cerberus-prometheus"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(slo:availability:objective, service_name)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "label": "Service",
        "multi": true,
        "name": "service",
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(slo:availability:objective, service_name)",
          "refId": "svc"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "type": "query"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Objectives are `clickhouse.slo` on the clickhouse node: availability is server spans without an error, latency server spans faster than the service's threshold, over a 28-day window. ClickHouse computes them every minute (`otel_slo`) and writes them back as `slo:*` series, from the same views vmalert's SLO rules read, so this dashboard and the alerts agree. A burn rate of 1 spends the whole budget in exactly 28 days. The rules page at 14.4 over 1h and 6 over 6h, and open a ticket at 1 over 3d, each only while the shorter window (5m, 30m, 6h) agrees."
      }
    },
